The issue is that tonic expects a stream of incoming connections, not a single connection. For a stdin/stdout or UnixStream::pair() setup, wrap your single stream in a one-shot stream using tokio_stream::once(Ok(stream)) and pass it via Server::builder().serve_with_incoming(...). That lets the H2 layer handle multiplexed requests over the one pipe without tonic wanting more connections.

